    "title": "VCU basketball: Location, March Madness history, more to know",
    "text": "ACCWhat to know about UNC basketball’s first-round March Madness opponent Rodd BaxleyFayetteville ObserverMarch 17, 2026, 5:31 a.m. ETUNC basketball is a No. 6 seed in the men’s 2026 NCAA Tournament and will face No. 11 seed VCU to tip off March Madness.The sixth-seeded Tar Heels (24-8) will take on the 11th-seeded Rams (27-7) on Thursday, March 19 in Greenville, S.C. The game tips off at 6:50 p.m. ET and will be televised on TNT. The winner will face No. 3 seed Illinois (24-8) or No. 14 seed Penn (18-11) in the round of 32 on Saturday, March 21.Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
